  "scope": {
    "native": "Same synthetic RGBA16F color/RG16F motion fixture/controls/model. 128 frames/process; discard32; two processes/route/extent. GPU runner/Evaluate excludes upload/readback; debug enabled. Not game FPS. Arithmetic mean of two process medians. RGBA16F color and RG16F motion textures on both routes.",
    "portable": "Per-route process/sample counts and measurement dates are recorded in each row. Medians of process medians, excluding warmup. Fractional motion (+0.375,-0.625), eight global blocks, one pass. Full call includes CPU preparation/history, transfers, inference, resolve and broker overhead; startup and file I/O excluded. GPU model time uses grouped GPU timing; CPU model time uses host timing. Native uses a different fixture/boundary. These are not in-game FPS results.",
    "memory": "Process host commitment, working set, and owned allocations are overlapping scopes, not quantities to add. Native DXGI residency includes the benchmark harness. Portable graph allocation bytes are provider-owned buffer requests, not whole-process GPU residency.",
    "validation": "Saved Phoenix regression hashes plus direct NVIDIA reset/final comparison on native fixture. Portable output hashes checked on saved fixtures and repeated history sequences across processes. No claim of portable/native identical output or live-game FPS.",
    "host_memory": "Whole-probe observations, not matched runner-only RAM. Phoenix retains weight/fixture host caches through the loop; NVIDIA uses transient host upload planes. Private commit and working set overlap GPU/driver allocations."
  },
